# novadeck: take Lepton's Android guest OFF zink and onto the freedreno gallium driver.
#
# WHY. liblepton/properties.sh writes `mesa.loader.driver.override=zink` into the guest's props
# whenever the mesa path is selected (i.e. unless LEPTON_FORCE_SOFTWARE=true), so GLES is meant to
# be zink-over-Turnip.
#
# ZINK NOW RUNS, BUT FLICKERS. Since packages/mesa-android builds Turnip with
# -Dandroid-strict=false (and packages/fossilize-android replaced the stub layer), the guest boots
# and renders on zink -- `RenderEngine: renderer : zink Vulkan 1.4(Turnip Adreno (TM) 750)`. But
# black bars flash across the frame, mostly on the right, on the Android desktop and in-game.
# Measured on a Pocket FIT 2026-10-01: gone with this override, and STILL THERE with Valve's own
# Frame-image guest Mesa -- so it is not our Mesa build but how a zink frame reaches the panel on
# our host stack (no implicit write fence on Turnip's buffers; Lepton's composer returns no release
# fences). Until that is fixed, the guest stays on freedreno.
#
# HISTORY: before -Dandroid-strict=false, zink could not create a screen at all (it lost
# VK_KHR_maintenance5), and the failure was fatal to the whole guest:
#
#     W MESA-EGL: DRI2: failed to create screen / Failed to open any DRM device
#     W libEGL  : eglInitialize(...) failed (EGL_NOT_INITIALIZED)
#     F RenderEngine: eglQueryStringImplementationANDROID(EGL_VERSION) failed
#     -> SurfaceFlinger never registers -> ServiceManager blocks -> libc++abi: terminating (pid 1)
#
# The container then dies ~4s in, which ALSO takes down adbd before it can open its listener --
# so the visible symptom is an APK install that fails with `adb: device offline`, nowhere near the
# actual cause. Measured on a Pocket S2 (Adreno 750), 2026-08-23.
#
# `msm` is the kernel driver name freedreno registers under, and it is what mesa's loader wants
# here. With this one property changed and nothing else, the same image goes from a 4-second death
# to a fully booted guest:
#
#     I RenderEngine: vendor: freedreno | renderer: FD750 | version: OpenGL ES 3.2 Mesa 26.2.1
#     I SurfaceFlinger: Boot is finished (2207 ms)
#     -> adb connects, `Performing Streamed Install` -> Success, UnityPlayerActivity starts
#
# WHY A PROPERTY AND NOT A PATCH. Lepton is a Steam app (3029110); any edit to liblepton is
# overwritten on update. The override is NOT a `ro.` property, so a later setprop wins -- and this
# slot is ours, so an init script here is the durable place to do it. Lepton bind-mounts every file
# under /usr/share/guestos/android at its matching absolute path, which lands this at
# /vendor/etc/init/novadeck-gfx.rc, where Android's init parses it.
#
# BOTH TRIGGERS ARE DELIBERATE, and this is the configuration that was actually validated on
# hardware. A `getprop` sampled 2s in still read `zink` while the value was `msm` by the time
# SurfaceFlinger started, so which of the two landed was never attributed. `setprop` is idempotent;
# shipping only one of them would be an untested configuration for no gain.
#
# REMOVE THIS when zink frames reach the panel without the black bars (or Lepton stops forcing
# zink) -- at which point tests/test-android-guestos.sh and rootfs/lib-assemble-storage.sh need
# their matching checks dropped too.
on early-init
    setprop mesa.loader.driver.override msm

on post-fs
    setprop mesa.loader.driver.override msm
